cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "safespec-raise: 长上下文推测解码的收益判据与增量回退调度（参考实现）"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of a falsifiable break-even criterion for long-context
  speculative decoding, together with RAISE, a scheduling scheme targeted at the
  dominant cause of slowdown (the extra target forward pass on mismatched rounds).
  Key finding: under the invariant of exactly one target forward pass per round,
  draft depth k is not an independent gain lever; long-context slowdown is
  determined by the per-round fixed overhead of the execution path, not by the
  speculative decoding mechanism itself.
authors:
